# AI Civ training situations v1
# Machine row format: correct_output_slot|candidate_output_slots|nonzero_input_slots|target_output_slots|short_description
# Comment blocks explain the game meaning of each slot used by the following machine row.
# situation 0: strategy budget case: zero funds sets zero science
# Purpose: teach Strategy output[67] as science funding ratio, not as military production demand.
# Budget rule: when funds are below 50, science funding should be proportional to funds/50; at 50 or more funds, science funding should be 1.0.
# Browser application: output[67] is converted to GameState.scienceRate percentage by multiplying by 100.
# input[966] = 0.000000 means legacy money account normalized by 200.
# input[1001] = 0.000000 means money account clamped to 0..50 and normalized to 0..1; this is the primary budget input.
# input[1002] = -0.300000 means recent account delta after income, upkeep, and technology expense.
# input[1003] = 0.600000 means upkeep burden signal.
# target[67] = 0.000000 means science funding ratio recommended by Strategy.
# Machine row below repeats the same situation in parser format.
67|67|1002:-0.300000,1003:0.600000||strategy budget case: zero funds sets zero science
